docs/plan.md:413:What: Three map facts with routing consequences. (a) The map's **closed thick-stroke polyline (~1.85 pt) is the sales-floor boundary** — everything outside (parking, drive-thru, curbside, Admin/Receiving/Loading Dock) is non-walkable; found automatically on both #659 (19 vertices) and #24 (11 vertices). (b) **Service areas (deli/bakery islands, seafood counters, pharmacy, kitchen, Meal Simple prep) are drawn as open floor** but are staff-only; their counters leave drawn gaps of ~0.5–1 m (staff pass-throughs), while genuine customer openings are ≥~1.5 m. (c) Department labels print **inside** their service areas, so naive snapping puts stops in staff space.
